error[E0277]: `Vec<u8>` is not ordered: the ordering operators are answered over the integer types and text
  --> tests/ui/op_order_on_bytes.rs:13:49
   |
13 |     let _ = cipher.query(op::Lt, &vec![1u8, 2]).on(&blob_plan);
   |                                                 ^^ no ordering operator over this type
   |
   = help: the trait `Ordered` is not implemented for `Vec<u8>`
   = note: `Lt`, `Lte`, `Gt`, `Gte` and `Between` take `u8` to `u128`, `i8` to `i128`, or a `String`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Ordered`:
             i128
             i16
             i32
             i64
             i8
             std::string::String
             u128
             u16
           and $N others
   = note: required for `stack_encrypt::op::Lt` to implement `DefaultIndex<Vec<u8>>`
   = note: required for `ValuePlan<Vec<u8>, Indexed<stack_encrypt::Ore>>` to implement `Chooses<stack_encrypt::op::Lt, Vec<u8>, Whole>`
